Modified upstream files
-----------------------
Three changes only. Two are portability fixes required to build or test on
Windows; one adds a dev-only dependency used by the verification scripts.
None changes behaviour on POSIX systems, and none touches the library's public
API or runtime behaviour.

  rollup.config.js
      glob() returns platform-native path separators, so on Windows every
      plugin entry arrived as 'src\plugins\foo.ts' and the subsequent
      .replace('src/', 'dist/') matched nothing. Output paths stayed inside
      src/ and `npm run build` aborted with
      "Path of Typescript compiler option 'outDir' must be located inside the
      same directory as the Rollup 'file' option".
      Fix: normalise separators once, at the point the entries are collected
      (split(path.sep).join('/')).

  tsconfig.json
      Added "scripts/**/*.test.ts" to "exclude". Without it, any test file
      under scripts/ is compiled by `tsc`, which shifts the inferred rootDir
      and emits the whole source tree into dist/src/ instead of dist/,
      breaking the package exports map (verify-exports then reports missing
      targets such as dist/webaudio.js).

  package.json
      Added one devDependency: "playwright-core": "^1.56.0", used by
      tools/verify.mjs and tools/shots.mjs to drive a local Chromium for the
      browser acceptance tests. The published library has no dependencies and
      no runtime change; playwright-core is never imported by src/.

New repository-level files added by this derivative work:
  .gitattributes   (declares "* -text": no line-ending rewriting, so the
                    byte-identical upstream files stay byte-identical)
  .gitignore       (adds shots/verify/, _diag/, deliver5/ to upstream's list)
  .github/workflows/pages.yml   (builds the library and publishes the demo)

Everything else under src/ (wavesurfer.ts, renderer.ts, player.ts, plugins/*,
state/*, reactive/*, the entire upstream test suite) is byte-identical to
upstream v8.0.3.

Third-party assets
------------------
The demo audio in demo/audio/ is generated by scripts/make-demo-audio.mjs at
build time. It contains no third-party recordings or samples. It is released
under CC0-1.0.

No other third-party code was added: the implementation uses only the
upstream FFT (src/fft.ts) and the standard DOM/Web Audio APIs.
